# semacs licensing

semacs is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
option) any later version (SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later). The full terms are in
LICENSE-GPL. This program is distributed WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; see that license.

Third-party source retains its own copyright and license. In particular, the
Apache-2.0 files listed in THIRD_PARTY.md remain under Apache-2.0; their license
and upstream copyright notice are in LICENSE-APACHE. This project-level notice
does not relicense those files.

When conveying binaries, provide the corresponding source, including local
modifications, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and the scripts needed to build it, in a
manner allowed by GPLv3 section 6. Include this notice, THIRD_PARTY.md and the
applicable license texts. Dependencies retain their respective license and
notice requirements; a binary release must audit and include those notices as
well. The local Zed checkout is not required to build semacs.
